WEBVTT

00:11.900 --> 00:13.240
ROY MUSTANG: The Freezing Alchemist?

00:13.440 --> 00:15.060
Really? He's here?

00:15.100 --> 00:18.780
BRADLEY: We have information that he managed
to slip into Central a few days ago.

00:18.980 --> 00:20.940
That's why I've summoned you here, Colonel.

00:21.080 --> 00:23.880
I need you and your men to smoke
him out and bring him in.

00:23.920 --> 00:25.320
Consider it done, sir.

00:25.320 --> 00:26.240
[BRADLEY CHUCKLES]

00:26.260 --> 00:28.720
BRADLEY: I'm glad you're with us in Central
for awhile, Mustang.

00:28.720 --> 00:30.900
It's good to know I have
people here I can count on.

00:30.980 --> 00:32.880
- Sir.
- Uh, one last thing...

00:32.940 --> 00:34.960
Our rising young star is here as well.

00:34.980 --> 00:36.920
I'm placing him at your disposal.

00:37.020 --> 00:40.620
Forgive me, Fuhrer Bradley,
but just to be clear, are you referring to...

00:40.620 --> 00:41.760
I am.

00:41.800 --> 00:45.200
I am the Fullmetal Alchemist, Edward Elric.

00:45.780 --> 00:46.860
Ah, damn it.

00:46.920 --> 00:49.260
The Colonel's never gonna
let us out of here, is he?

00:49.540 --> 00:52.160
We already bought
our tickets for Liore, too.

00:52.200 --> 00:53.760
Does this mean we're not going?

00:53.760 --> 00:55.460
I don't know, Al.

00:55.640 --> 00:57.600
For now, let's just get this over with.

00:57.600 --> 00:58.720
- Okay?
- Mmm.

00:58.860 --> 01:00.040
Lead the way, brother.

01:00.180 --> 01:03.660
Kono omoi wo keshite shimau niwa

01:03.660 --> 01:06.000
mada jinsei nagai dsho?

01:06.980 --> 01:12.440
Yarinokoshite'ru koto
yarinaoshite mitai kara

01:22.200 --> 01:28.440
Yume no tsuzuki oikakete ita hazu na no ni

01:28.760 --> 01:34.780
Magarikunetta
hosoi michi hito ni tsumazuku

01:34.780 --> 01:41.700
Ano koro mitai ni tte modoritai wake ja nai ni
Nakushite kita sora wo sagashite'ru

01:41.700 --> 01:43.320
Wakatte kuremasu you ni

01:43.320 --> 01:48.480
Gisei ni natta you na
kanashii kao wa yamete yo

01:48.480 --> 01:51.940
Tsumi no saigo wa namida ja nai yo
Zutto kurushiku seotte'ku n da

01:51.940 --> 01:55.320
Deguchi mienai kanjou meiro ni
dare wo matte'ru no?

01:55.320 --> 01:58.900
Shiroi nooto ni tsuzutta you ni
motto sunao ni hakidashitai yo

01:58.900 --> 02:02.040
Nani kar nogaretai n da
genjitsu tte yatsu?

02:02.040 --> 02:08.740
Kanaeru tame ni ikite'ru n datte
Sakebitaku naru yo Kikoete imasu ka?

02:08.760 --> 02:13.840
Bunai n nante yatte'rarenai kara

02:13.880 --> 02:15.720
...kaeru basho mo nai no

02:15.720 --> 02:19.020
Yasashisa niwa itsumo kansha shite'ru

02:19.020 --> 02:22.500
Dakara tsuyoku naritai
(I'm on the way)

02:22.500 --> 02:26.160
Natsukashiku naru
konna itami mo kangei jan

02:26.160 --> 02:29.680

02:29.860 --> 02:33.200
[WHISTLE BLOWING]

02:33.200 --> 02:34.240
[FOOTSTEPS]

02:34.900 --> 02:36.420
There he goes, that way!

02:36.420 --> 02:38.540
You, halt! Halt or I'll shoot!

02:40.860 --> 02:42.160
[YELLING]

02:48.140 --> 02:49.100
Ah!

02:52.480 --> 02:53.560
[BODY THUDS]

02:53.820 --> 02:55.620
Water freezes, water boils.

02:55.780 --> 02:57.440
Either way, you're just as dead.

03:02.160 --> 03:03.220
That's alchemy.

03:03.960 --> 03:05.820
ED: What a nasty thing to do.

03:06.580 --> 03:09.920
You of all people should know,
great deeds required great sacrifice.

03:10.100 --> 03:12.340
Isn't that the law equivalent exchange?

03:12.420 --> 03:15.600
Save your breath, the laws of alchemy
don't justify murder!

03:23.860 --> 03:25.540
No transmutation circle!

03:25.740 --> 03:27.400
Don't be too impressed.

03:27.400 --> 03:28.640
Now!

03:38.180 --> 03:39.020
What?!

03:40.360 --> 03:43.300
No, I had you!
Any water there should've boiled!

03:43.460 --> 03:46.540
If it's any consolation,
you did ruin my coat.

03:48.040 --> 03:49.420
An automail arm!

03:52.800 --> 03:54.900
A young gifted alchemist...

03:55.100 --> 03:57.760
One who doesn't use transmutation circles...

03:58.020 --> 04:00.380
And who has an auto mail right arm!

04:00.780 --> 04:02.440
I know you.

04:02.520 --> 04:06.960
You are the Fullmetal Alchemist,
Edward Elric!

04:10.340 --> 04:11.780
So...it's not you?

04:11.780 --> 04:13.540
Oh...um, no!

04:13.640 --> 04:15.600
I'm his younger brother, Alphonse.

04:15.620 --> 04:16.960
But he's a runt!

04:16.960 --> 04:18.620
Oh, yeah?! Can runt do this?!

04:23.440 --> 04:26.760
I've heard the stories,
but still I never imagined this.

04:26.760 --> 04:29.460
The Fullmetal Alchemist
is just a little kid!

04:29.780 --> 04:31.800
Don't call me little!

04:32.660 --> 04:37.060
You know brother, I don't think he was
really talking about your height just now.

04:37.420 --> 04:39.720
Well even if he wasn't, he still pissed me off!

04:40.300 --> 04:42.760
So you're the one we've been
hearing all the stories about lately!

04:42.760 --> 04:44.240
The Fullmetal Alchemist!

04:44.480 --> 04:46.420
You're as good as they say,
thanks for the help.

04:46.660 --> 04:48.840
Um, you're welcome, but...

04:48.840 --> 04:51.180
I'm really not the one you should be thanking.

04:51.180 --> 04:52.460
There.

04:52.840 --> 04:54.480
C'mon, let's get going Al.

04:54.480 --> 04:55.660
We got a train to catch.

04:55.660 --> 04:59.240
Oh, okay! Um...
if you think it's alright to leave...

05:03.400 --> 05:04.140
[THUD]

05:04.240 --> 05:05.140
[GASPS]

05:10.000 --> 05:11.440
What is that?! Steam?

05:11.440 --> 05:13.020
Brother, he's gone!

05:13.660 --> 05:16.040
Damn it, now he really pissed me off!

05:17.360 --> 05:20.840
MUSTANG: Looks like you underestimated
your opponent, Fullmetal.

05:21.080 --> 05:23.060
Who is this guy anyway?

05:23.140 --> 05:25.960
You'd know that if you'd listen
to the briefing like I told you to.

05:26.140 --> 05:28.740
But no, you had to go
charging right after him—

05:28.740 --> 05:31.920
Yeah, yeah, I get it, alright?
I'm sorry, 'kay? Whatever.

05:32.960 --> 05:36.040
Next time a superior tells you
to pay attention, you might just try it.

05:36.820 --> 05:37.500
Fine.

05:37.900 --> 05:40.740
Now then, his name is Isaac McDougal.

05:41.000 --> 05:44.240
Or he was known back in the day,
Isaac the Freezer.

05:44.380 --> 05:46.240
He's a former State Alchemist.

05:46.400 --> 05:47.340
ED: Former?

05:47.740 --> 05:51.000
That's right.
He served in the Ishvalan war.

05:51.320 --> 05:55.260
During that time, he gave us
no signs that he'd turned traitor.

05:56.260 --> 06:00.260
But after, he immediately resigned
his commission and went into hiding.

06:00.480 --> 06:03.720
He's been working with the
anti-establishment movement ever since.

06:03.840 --> 06:07.020
Taking him into custody
is a matter of top priority.

06:07.460 --> 06:09.980
Whether it's dead or alive,
that's up to him.

06:10.160 --> 06:12.320
No way, I'm not killing anyone for you.

06:12.540 --> 06:14.100
And that's your choice.

06:14.360 --> 06:16.640
Your orders are simply to
help us contain him.

06:16.840 --> 06:17.800
That's all.

06:20.470 --> 06:22.440
[CHUCKLES] Off topic...

06:22.660 --> 06:25.740
Have you turned up any leads
for getting your bodies back to normal?

06:27.140 --> 06:29.400
Maybe if you ever gave us time to look!

06:29.600 --> 06:31.100
Roy! How goes?

06:31.120 --> 06:33.840
Heard you let him put you in
charge of catching the Freezer, huh?

06:33.840 --> 06:35.460
One hell of an nasty assignment.

06:35.540 --> 06:38.540
But hey, could be your chance
to earn that promotion to Central.

06:38.540 --> 06:41.120
Oh, say!
Looks like my timing was perfect!

06:41.140 --> 06:42.880
You two are the Elric brothers, right?

06:43.040 --> 06:43.660
ED: Huh?

06:43.680 --> 06:46.840
Wow, it's an honor to finally meet
the youngest State Alchemist ever.

06:46.860 --> 06:48.240
You're a real legend around here!

06:48.280 --> 06:50.300
I'm Lieutenant Colonel Maes Hughes, a pleasure.

06:50.300 --> 06:52.020
Um...you want Edward!

06:52.020 --> 06:54.280
I'm actually his younger brother, Alphonse.

06:54.280 --> 06:57.740
What?! You're the Fullmetal Alchemist?
Sorry, I had no idea you would be so...

06:57.740 --> 07:00.360
Go on, say little. I dare you.

07:00.400 --> 07:01.320
MUSTANG: Hughes.

07:01.320 --> 07:02.100
Yeah?

07:02.140 --> 07:04.140
What are you doing here?
Go home.

07:04.200 --> 07:07.000
Actually, I'm here on official business.

07:07.260 --> 07:10.580
You, Elrics, I understand that
you two don't have a place to stay.

07:10.860 --> 07:12.520
Which means you'll have to come with me.

07:12.520 --> 07:13.420
BOTH: Huh?

07:15.240 --> 07:16.200
BOTH: Ah!

07:19.860 --> 07:23.300
My wife, Gracia and my daughter, Elicia.
We'd love to have you!

07:24.660 --> 07:26.460
Hi, Princess!
[ELICIA GIGGLING]

07:27.160 --> 07:30.280
Ow! Daddy, your beard is itchy!
[LAUGHS]

07:31.340 --> 07:32.160
Like this?

07:32.160 --> 07:35.420
Itchy! Itchy!
[BOTH GIGGLING]

07:36.500 --> 07:39.540
HUGHES: Look, we have guests!
These are the Elric brothers.

07:40.500 --> 07:42.080
Big brother!

07:42.220 --> 07:43.980
Little brother!

07:44.680 --> 07:47.700
Nice to meet you. My name is Edward Elric.

07:47.880 --> 07:50.480
This is my younger brother, Alphonse Elric.

07:50.480 --> 07:51.620
Get that?

07:51.640 --> 07:53.820
[EMPHASIZING] Young-er broth-er.

07:53.820 --> 07:56.520
But younger means little...
You're little!

07:57.700 --> 07:59.320
AL: Just let it go Ed...
ED: Where do you get off calling me little?!

07:59.320 --> 08:01.600
AL: These people are being nice to let us stay here!
ED: You look in the mirror lately?!

08:01.620 --> 08:04.840
HUGHES: Hope you boys are hungry.
Gracia's cooking his delicious!

08:05.160 --> 08:05.900
Huh?!

08:08.080 --> 08:09.180
ED: Ah...!
[ELICIA GIGGLING]

08:09.180 --> 08:10.300
Okay, eat up.

08:11.280 --> 08:12.320
Thanks!

08:13.880 --> 08:16.760
Wow, you weren't kidding!
This is great!

08:16.880 --> 08:19.000
GRACIA: Don't be shy. Eat all you want!

08:19.000 --> 08:20.240
ED: Okay!
AL: [GIGGLES]

08:21.140 --> 08:24.560
Alphonse, how you're going to eat
wearing that armor? Take it off, relax!

08:24.560 --> 08:26.440
BOTH: Uh...

08:26.480 --> 08:27.900
Well, you see...uh—

08:27.900 --> 08:30.320
He's not allowed to!
He has to wear it all the time.

08:30.320 --> 08:32.720
It's uh...
It's part of his alchemy training!

08:32.740 --> 08:33.920
[NERVOUS LAUGH]
You know how it is.

08:33.920 --> 08:35.420
I'll eat enough for both of us.

08:35.420 --> 08:37.300
Training, choo-choo!

08:39.500 --> 08:41.500
Translation: "Central Prison"
[MAN LAUGHING]

08:41.520 --> 08:45.940
KIMBLEE: Hands down that's got to be the funniest
joke I've heard in a long, long time.

08:46.260 --> 08:49.620
The Freezing Alchemist wants
me to come play his sidekick.

08:49.820 --> 08:51.340
Well as fun as that sounds,

08:51.520 --> 08:54.180
The Crimson Alchemist works alone,
I always have.

08:54.400 --> 09:00.000
Kimblee, if we work together we can bring
down Bradley and his godforsaken military.

09:00.300 --> 09:02.940
You saw the horrors
that took place in Ishval

09:02.960 --> 09:04.480
You were there, dammit!

09:04.580 --> 09:06.880
You know the things
Bradley ordered us to do.

09:06.880 --> 09:08.640
The kind of man he really is.

09:08.760 --> 09:12.220
That's why you killed all those officers, isn't it?
To send him a message?

09:12.240 --> 09:14.120
[CACKLING]

09:14.140 --> 09:16.260
I think you've got me all wrong.

09:16.480 --> 09:20.400
My motives aren't so sophisticated
as revenge or honor any of that.

09:20.480 --> 09:24.140
The reason I killed all of those men
was because I could.

09:24.520 --> 09:25.520
It's that simple.

09:26.360 --> 09:28.420
That's too bad, Kimblee.
[FOOTSTEPS LEAVING]

09:28.500 --> 09:30.240
That truly is too bad.

09:31.140 --> 09:35.350
[PRISON DOORS OPEN AND CLOSING]

09:35.900 --> 09:37.460
Keep up the good work.

09:38.860 --> 09:40.420
[BODY SMASHES]

09:46.000 --> 09:48.740
[DOOR OPENS]
Maes, dear...what's wrong?

09:48.740 --> 09:49.920
Can't sleep?

09:49.940 --> 09:50.920
Guess not.

09:56.080 --> 09:57.660
I know it's in that head of yours.

09:58.460 --> 10:00.280
You're worrying about
those boys, aren't you?

10:02.160 --> 10:04.500
You do know what they call
State Alchemists, right?

10:04.500 --> 10:07.800
The dogs of the military,
not exactly the most popular bunch.

10:08.080 --> 10:11.520
I try to imagine what that must be like,
enduring that at his age.

10:16.040 --> 10:17.980
Brother, you awake?

10:18.340 --> 10:19.160
Huh?

10:19.180 --> 10:20.720
Miss Gracia's quiche...

10:20.720 --> 10:22.780
It looked a lot like moms, huh?

10:22.920 --> 10:25.040
Yeah, almost as good too.

10:25.040 --> 10:25.700
Really?!

10:26.020 --> 10:30.460
In that case, I'm definitely adding it to the list
of things I'm gonna eat once I get my body back!

10:30.920 --> 10:31.640
Right.

10:31.720 --> 10:33.740
Put it on there, right near the top.

10:34.020 --> 10:34.860
AL: Brother?

10:35.140 --> 10:35.720
ED: Hmm?

10:36.360 --> 10:39.300
AL: I sure would like to get
our old bodies back soon.

10:39.840 --> 10:42.020
ED: I know. Me too.

10:46.640 --> 10:47.960
MCDOUGAL: One more.

10:48.580 --> 10:52.880
One more and Fuhrer
Bradley is on his way to hell.

10:53.740 --> 10:55.280
Fullmetal Alchemist

10:57.080 --> 10:58.580
Fullmetal Alchemist

11:00.300 --> 11:04.280
MUSTANG: We have a confirmed report that
McDougal broke into Central Prison last night.

11:04.720 --> 11:06.920
Whatever he's up to, he's growing bold.

11:06.960 --> 11:08.520
That means our time is short.

11:09.500 --> 11:12.860
Close off all roads,
search every square inch of the city.

11:13.000 --> 11:15.440
When you find him, shoot on sight.

11:15.460 --> 11:18.050
That is an order from the Fuhrer himself.

11:19.600 --> 11:21.780
But if I find him first...

11:21.820 --> 11:22.660
He's mine.

11:22.740 --> 11:24.320
Get a medic! Hurry!

11:24.360 --> 11:26.580
Report to headquarters!
Five men dead!

11:26.720 --> 11:27.900
How awful.

11:27.920 --> 11:29.500
It looks like a steam explosion.

11:29.600 --> 11:33.460
Raise the temperature of water fast enough
it expands with the force of a bomb blast.

11:33.620 --> 11:36.020
And the human body is 70% water.

11:36.920 --> 11:37.880
Let's hurry.

11:37.880 --> 11:39.840
We have to find him
before he hurts anyone else.

11:39.840 --> 11:40.680
Mmm!

11:43.060 --> 11:44.080
Finished.

11:47.140 --> 11:51.640
Impressive reflexes, Isaac,
few are able to dodge my alchemy so easily!

11:51.660 --> 11:52.740
I know that voice.

11:52.800 --> 11:54.100
Is that you, Armstrong?

11:54.640 --> 11:55.900
Indeed!

11:56.180 --> 11:57.240
None other.

12:00.080 --> 12:02.840
It is I, the Strong Arm Alchemist,

12:02.920 --> 12:05.820
Alex Louis Armstrong, in the flesh!

12:05.980 --> 12:07.220
Ah, shut it!

12:09.940 --> 12:12.920
I've always wanted to
chop that ego down to size.

12:14.940 --> 12:18.680
Except you'll need far more
than water to quench my fists!

12:20.340 --> 12:21.540
[GASPS]

12:26.360 --> 12:27.440
AL: Major!

12:32.940 --> 12:34.860
The water from his canteen, huh?

12:35.000 --> 12:36.780
Thanks for the quick save, Al.

12:37.500 --> 12:39.080
Let's go, he's getting away.

12:39.120 --> 12:41.140
Come then, after me, Elric Brothers.

12:41.180 --> 12:42.540
BOTH: Right!

12:49.800 --> 12:52.160
It's been a long time, Freezer.

12:54.060 --> 12:55.760
MCDOUGAL: Well, Roy Mustang.

12:55.760 --> 12:56.500
Heh.

12:56.740 --> 12:59.040
So the Flame Alchemist came out to play.

12:59.040 --> 13:00.840
MUSTANG: You can make this easy on both of us.

13:00.840 --> 13:02.680
I'd rather not fight an old war buddy.

13:02.700 --> 13:05.720
War buddy? Please,
don't flatter yourself.

13:05.960 --> 13:07.660
I knew no friends in Ishval.

13:07.700 --> 13:10.420
Only military bastards,
and their damn dogs!

13:18.440 --> 13:21.540
When water meets flame,
the flame goes out.

13:29.860 --> 13:31.400
Dammit, ugh!

13:34.780 --> 13:36.640
Still there! Perfect!

13:36.780 --> 13:38.080
Stop right there!

13:38.460 --> 13:42.040
I was wondering what you were doing
in this alley, so I came back to check it out,

13:42.060 --> 13:43.200
And bingo!

13:43.440 --> 13:45.200
[MCDOUGAL LAUGHS]

13:46.100 --> 13:48.020
There's nowhere to run this time!

13:48.060 --> 13:50.240
Clearly, but who's running?

13:58.840 --> 13:59.980
[GASPS]

14:01.820 --> 14:03.200
An alchemic reaction...

14:03.280 --> 14:04.780
On this scale...

14:05.260 --> 14:07.460
Impossible! Unless...

14:07.640 --> 14:08.780
- AL: You don't think he's...?

14:09.580 --> 14:11.500
A Philosopher's Stone!

14:17.520 --> 14:19.720
He's freezing all the moisture in the air.

14:19.740 --> 14:21.340
Edward, Elric.

14:21.460 --> 14:24.520
You've sworn your life to the state
as a dog of the military,

14:25.440 --> 14:26.180
But...

14:26.180 --> 14:28.920
Do you really know the ones you serve
or what their true plans are?

14:28.980 --> 14:31.220
Who cares?!
It's not my problem.

14:31.240 --> 14:32.240
Don't be a fool!

14:32.280 --> 14:35.220
He'll lead us to all ruin!
I'm only doing what needs to be done!

14:35.340 --> 14:37.300
I told you, I don't care!

14:46.060 --> 14:47.800
All right! Nice work, Al.

14:47.820 --> 14:49.920
AL: But we still have to stop his alchemy!

14:49.960 --> 14:50.800
ED: I know.

14:50.800 --> 14:52.200
So where is it?

14:52.280 --> 14:54.540
You have a Philosopher's Stone,
don't you?

14:54.580 --> 14:56.180
What are you talking about?

14:56.260 --> 14:58.480
I won't ask again. Where is it?!

14:58.520 --> 15:00.520
And what are you going to do, boy?

15:00.620 --> 15:02.100
You're out of your league!

15:11.000 --> 15:12.180
Ahh!

15:12.180 --> 15:15.660
Stand back and prepare for a
display of Armstrong alchemy!

15:15.680 --> 15:17.180
He's all yours, Major!

15:17.360 --> 15:23.060
Witness the alchemic art passed
down the Armstrong line for generations!

15:27.900 --> 15:29.100
That's unexpected!

15:29.100 --> 15:31.180
What the heck are you doing?!
You're making it worse!

15:31.180 --> 15:32.900
No! I was merely—
[BOOM]

15:37.080 --> 15:38.460
AL: The ice walls...

15:38.480 --> 15:39.800
They're merging!

15:39.980 --> 15:41.820
But, that would mean...

15:42.760 --> 15:44.600
ED: If they all meet in the middle...

15:44.740 --> 15:47.440
Ah, damn it!
It's Central Command!

15:47.660 --> 15:49.600
BOTH: He's gonna freeze it over!

15:51.280 --> 15:52.060
Major!

15:52.080 --> 15:53.880
Al and I'll try to slow him down.

15:53.920 --> 15:55.960
Can you handle the transmutation circles?

15:55.960 --> 15:58.200
Consider them erased. I'm on it.

16:01.520 --> 16:03.100
Fuhrer King Bradley,

16:03.100 --> 16:06.800
For your cold-blooded crimes in Ishval,
I condemn you to a frozen hell.

16:06.800 --> 16:08.320
- Not so fast!
- Huh?!

16:19.040 --> 16:20.380
Two can play that game!

16:26.700 --> 16:28.680
[ED YELPING]

16:29.200 --> 16:30.280
Brother!

16:30.280 --> 16:31.440
Too slow!

16:34.840 --> 16:35.860
Alphonse!

16:45.500 --> 16:47.540
There's no one in there...
It's empty!

16:48.960 --> 16:53.240
But that...that could only be true
if his soul was bonded to the armor.

16:54.100 --> 16:55.960
So you lost your arm,

16:55.960 --> 16:59.120
and your brother, he lost his entire body?

16:59.420 --> 17:00.300
Heh.

17:00.480 --> 17:02.840
I see. It all makes sense.

17:04.180 --> 17:06.940
You fools committed the ultimate taboo!

17:07.680 --> 17:10.560
You attempted human
transmutation, didn't you?

17:10.580 --> 17:13.480
Alchemy's one and only unforgivable sin!

17:15.840 --> 17:18.540
[SCREAMING] Al!

17:18.680 --> 17:21.680
Dammit! This can't be happening!

17:22.180 --> 17:23.340
No!

17:23.460 --> 17:25.520
He's gone! What I have done?!

17:27.900 --> 17:29.200
[VOICE TREMBLING]
Give him back...

17:29.240 --> 17:30.580
He's my brother!

17:30.980 --> 17:32.460
Just give him back!

17:32.600 --> 17:35.760
He's my little brother.
He's all I have left!

17:42.260 --> 17:43.140
Y'know...

17:43.440 --> 17:46.280
there are some lines you
really shouldn't cross.

17:46.920 --> 17:47.760
[FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING]

18:05.260 --> 18:06.280
ED: Give it up!

18:06.300 --> 18:08.280
There's no water for you to use here.

18:08.280 --> 18:10.220
[LAUGHS]
You've forgotten something.

18:10.260 --> 18:13.440
I have all the water I need...
70% of my body!

18:13.440 --> 18:14.300
[GASPS]

18:15.820 --> 18:16.880
Ed!

18:21.120 --> 18:22.920
Why can't you fools understand?

18:22.920 --> 18:24.800
I'm trying to save this country!

18:30.980 --> 18:34.500
[CACKLING]

18:35.320 --> 18:36.310
Brother...

18:36.600 --> 18:37.440
Brother!

18:37.540 --> 18:39.720
Come on. We're going after him.

18:39.940 --> 18:41.440
I'm not done.

18:42.840 --> 18:43.920
Not even close.

18:46.900 --> 18:48.020
Did we get it?

18:48.020 --> 18:48.980
[GASPS]

18:50.300 --> 18:51.460
Not again!

18:56.900 --> 18:59.920
What do you think of my flames
now, you bastard?!

19:00.900 --> 19:02.320
When will he learn?

19:02.580 --> 19:04.980
It's bad enough that he's useless on rainy days.

19:11.900 --> 19:12.420
Huh?

19:13.780 --> 19:15.060
Bradley.

19:18.260 --> 19:22.620
[CACKLING MADLY]

19:22.920 --> 19:24.060
Perfect!

19:39.420 --> 19:45.620
[CONTINUES CACKLING]

20:04.600 --> 20:05.200
[KIMBLEE CHUCKLES]

20:07.200 --> 20:09.200
Now that is too bad.

20:09.640 --> 20:10.820
Major, go now!

20:10.880 --> 20:12.000
Leave it to me!

20:12.000 --> 20:15.660
The Armstrong fist will not fail!

20:31.040 --> 20:34.700
[ED PANTING]

20:36.660 --> 20:39.000
ED: Fuhrer Bradley...You're here?

20:39.140 --> 20:41.440
Ah, yes!
Job well done, Fullmetal.

20:41.460 --> 20:43.520
I came out to see if I could lend a hand.

20:43.940 --> 20:45.340
And to think...

20:45.460 --> 20:47.760
that I'd actually
be the one to catch him.

20:48.400 --> 20:51.460
If nothing else, this should
make an exciting story for my son!

20:53.280 --> 20:54.300
[SNEEZE]

20:54.500 --> 20:56.120
HUGHES: Ooh, is that a cold I hear?

20:56.150 --> 20:59.220
Ah, never mind! From what I'm told
you're the man of the hour!

20:59.340 --> 21:02.360
Nah, I just destroyed
the transmutation circles.

21:02.440 --> 21:05.020
The Fuhrer is the one who
actually brought down McDougal.

21:05.220 --> 21:07.700
Sure, but the Fuhrer's
telling everyone it was you!

21:07.700 --> 21:09.200
So congratulations!

21:09.580 --> 21:10.980
Oh, it's like that, huh?

21:11.060 --> 21:13.400
Suit yourself, but some friendly advice...

21:13.400 --> 21:18.440
Next time a superior tells you to take credit
for something you didn't do, you might try it for once.

21:22.660 --> 21:23.620
We never did find out whether
or not he had a Philosopher's Stone.
AL: You know...

21:23.620 --> 21:27.000
We never did find out whether
or not he had a Philosopher's Stone.

21:27.060 --> 21:30.160
No, but maybe it'll say
something in the official report.

21:30.160 --> 21:30.800
[KNOCKING AT DOOR]

21:31.960 --> 21:32.480
BOTH: Hmm?

21:32.480 --> 21:34.120
Greetings, Edward Elric.

21:34.260 --> 21:37.080
When I heard you were in the hospital,
I dashed right over!

21:37.100 --> 21:38.860
Ahh!
[BOTH WHIMPERING]

21:39.140 --> 21:42.720
And as I suspected, you're in
desperate need of my assistance.

21:42.720 --> 21:44.720
ARMSTRONG: A-ha!
[ED AND AL YELLING]

21:45.180 --> 21:50.140
ARMSTRONG: You need the example of a perfect
physical specimen to inspire your recovery!

21:50.180 --> 21:52.880
You see? You're looking lively already!

21:52.880 --> 21:54.920
ED: Will you get out!
[ARMSTRONG LAUGHING]

21:58.020 --> 22:00.640
Ah, I see. So Isaac's dead, is he?

22:00.960 --> 22:03.980
That's a shame. I had such
high hopes for him, too.

22:04.200 --> 22:06.440
But...the Philosopher's Stone?

22:07.400 --> 22:08.160
[CHUCKLES]

22:08.360 --> 22:10.060
Sounds like he overused it.

22:11.400 --> 22:14.750
Gluttony, try to chew
quietly, I'm on the phone.

22:15.960 --> 22:18.720
Yes, things are going well here in Liore.

22:19.500 --> 22:20.820
We'll be ready.

22:21.080 --> 22:23.460
It all begins very soon.

22:28.480 --> 22:34.300
Ano hi mita sora akaneiro no sora o

22:34.380 --> 22:39.600
nee kimi wa oboete imasu ka

22:39.660 --> 22:45.360
Yakusoku chigiri shoka
no kaze ga tsutsumu

22:45.620 --> 22:50.500
futari yorisotta

22:53.580 --> 22:58.760
Muri na egao no ura

22:58.760 --> 23:04.140
nobita kage o kakumau

23:04.180 --> 23:13.520
Dakara kizukanu furi saisei o erabu

23:15.600 --> 23:22.740
Table no ue no furuenai shirase machitsuzukete

23:26.160 --> 23:31.580
kuuhaku no yoru o kuru hazu no nai asa mo

23:31.580 --> 23:35.880
zenbu wakatte'tan da

23:35.960 --> 23:41.440
Ano hi mita sora akaneiro no sora o

23:41.440 --> 23:46.640
nee itsuka omoidasu deshou

23:46.640 --> 23:52.080
Hatasenakatta yakusoku o idaite

23:52.320 --> 23:57.140
futari arukidasu

24:00.720 --> 24:03.120
Resembool, a quiet town.

24:03.360 --> 24:08.340
The place where Edward and Alphonse were born.
The home they once shared with their mother.

24:09.260 --> 24:15.820
In the hopes of returning to happier times, the boys commit
the ultimate taboo and are forced to confront the truth.

24:16.420 --> 24:19.580
Next time on Fullmetal Alchemist: Brotherhood

24:19.580 --> 24:22.140
Episode 2: The First Day

24:23.880 --> 24:26.860
The day they resolved their hearts to begin the journey.
